/**
 * Active NBA Player Database — CAREER edition.
 *
 * The game evaluates each player's *whole career* as if they start over as a
 * rookie and play a normalized 15-season arc. So ratings here describe a
 * player's CAREER-PEAK ability (LeBron's prime, not age 41), and a set of
 * career attributes describe how that career plays out: when they peak, how
 * gracefully they age, how durable they are, whether they win, whether they
 * make teammates better, and whether they fit a team and a coach.
 *
 * Fields:
 *   id, name, age (current age — for flavor only), pos, eligible
 *
 *   ratings (0-100) — CAREER-PEAK skill profile:
 *     scoring, shooting, playmaking, rebounding,
 *     perimeterD, interiorD, athleticism, iq
 *
 *   injuryRisk (0-100) — career durability discount (history + body type).
 *
 *   career:
 *     earlyImpact   (0-100) how good they are right out of the gate
 *     aging         (0-100) how well the game ages / late-career longevity
 *     winning       (0-100) playoff performance + winning pedigree/clutch
 *     elevates      (0-100) makes teammates better & teams win
 *     ballDominance (0-100) needs the ball (high = harder to pair with alphas)
 *     culture       (0-100) locker-room/character (low = team cancer)
 *     coachability  (0-100) works within systems & with coaches
 *
 *   archetype — short label
 *
 * Ratings are subjective approximations for a draft game, not scouting truth.
 */

